 # spendlog
 
-A tiny command-line expense tracker.
+A tiny command-line expense tracker. Expenses are stored in a plain CSV file,
+so you can open them in any spreadsheet program.
+
+## Installation
+
+Requires Python 3.10 or newer.
+
+```bash
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+Record an expense (the date defaults to today):
+
+```bash
+spendlog add 12.50 food --note "lunch"
+spendlog add 2.40 transport --day 2026-03-20
+```
+
+List all expenses, or only one category:
+
+```bash
+spendlog list
+spendlog list --category food
+```
+
+Show the totals per category for one month:
+
+```bash
+spendlog report 2026-03
+```
+
+Expenses are saved to `expenses.csv` in the current directory. Pass
+`--file PATH` before the command to use a different file.
